  "ingredients": [
    "1 tablespoon kosher salt",
    "1.5 teaspoons ground black pepper",
    "1.5 teaspoons Cajun seasoning",
    "2.5 pounds chicken wings",
    "0.66666668653488 cup hot pepper sauce (such as Frank's RedHot®)",
    "0.5 cup butter",
    "1.5 tablespoons white vinegar",
    "0.5 teaspoon Worcestershire sauce",
    "0.125 teaspoon garlic powder",
    "1 pinch salt to taste"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Gather all ingredients. Heat a smoker to 225 degrees F (110 degrees C) according to the manufacturer’s directions.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/J8dX6H_u67pJ8fWZq9k-vYza5GM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-01-c63d3fe3a1f545868069f84dc80da52c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the dry rub: Mix 1 tablespoon salt, pepper, and Cajun seasoning in a small bowl; sprinkle over chicken wings.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/UkxnthhmRKtKAAkYo_bcF4VAfHM=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-02-9afdf0fb1d65418f85f3382d2e4b660c.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_02.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Place chicken wings, unstacked, onto wire racks. Place the racks into the smoker. Add wood chips according to the manufacturer’s directions; smoke chicken wings in the preheated smoker for 1 hour.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hyxCTUqgYHga-FV3flcyPoKLs30=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-03_2-75639dea4ee64216a4648b83fe975892.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "To make the sauce: Combine hot pepper sauce, butter, vinegar, Worcestershire sauce, garlic powder, and salt in a small saucepan over low heat. Cook, stirring often, until butter is melted and sauce is smooth; set aside.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/ca0AhLzYqrYCN0YwGCVjlnvu4Zc=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-04-68ec366fe0954742b9d673682bc3fea9.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat an outdoor grill for medium-high heat and lightly oil the grate. Transfer smoked wings to a large bowl; stir in 1/2 of the sauce until wings are evenly coated.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/Y__9Jwaw5O6mjdc3Jao1c9b673g=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-05-faf37c250b7a477098261ae7b2c2a371.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook wings on the preheated grill until skin is browned and crispy, about 4 to 5 minutes per side. An instant-read thermometer inserted near the bone should read 165 degrees F (74 degrees C). Transfer to a large bowl and stir in remaining sauce until wings are well coated.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/MuwZ6vm8sy0a-O07YToqYfWk0I0=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/AR-247276-Smoked-Chicken-Hot-WIngs-DDMFS-4x3-Step-06-83c9fe5f5300480abcac47f8d8b7cf17.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/247276/step_06.webp"
    }
  ],
